Description: Close several fail-open / unchecked-allocation paths
 - process_metachars() returned strdup(input) without a NULL check;
   callers assigned the result to nasty_metachars, and a NULL there
   silently DISABLED metachar filtering (contains_nasty_metachars
   returns FALSE for NULL). The config parser now treats an
   allocation failure as an error, and both initialization-time
   strdup()s abort instead of running unfiltered.
 - The fd_set for the accept loop's select() was re-calloc()d without
   a NULL check - an OOM would NULL-deref in FD_SET; now fatal.
 - conn_check_peer() had no default case in its address-family
   switch: a peer of an unexpected family (e.g. AF_UNIX under an
   inetd super-server) skipped allowed_hosts entirely. Such peers
   are now refused (fail closed).
 - conn_check_peer() returned after close() on getpeername() failure,
   letting the caller run handle_connection() on a dead descriptor
   and double-close it. It now exits like every other reject path.
 - nptr/nptr6 are now initialized to NULL (defensive; silences
   -Wanalyzer-use-of-uninitialized-value).
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
